cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >
  If you use this software or its experimental results,
  please cite the software using the metadata below.

type: software

title: >
  Robust Pixel-Wise Remote Sensing Classification: Multi-Criteria Feature
  Selection, Dyadic Quadrant Polling (DQP), and Machine Learning Benchmarks

abstract: >
  Research software and benchmarking suite for robust pixel-wise classification
  of remote sensing imagery (Sentinel-2) under severe sensor and environmental
  degradation (AWGN, Poisson, and Impulse Salt & Pepper noise). The framework
  integrates a 33-dimensional feature space combining raw spectral RGB values,
  Texture-Entropy-Gradient (TEG) descriptors, local 2D Discrete Cosine Transform
  (DCT) ring-energy features, and a novel asymmetric Dyadic Quadrant Polling (DQP)
  structural descriptor. It introduces an adaptive multi-criteria feature utility
  function (Mode B) balancing Information Gain, correlation redundancy discounting,
  and feature extraction time penalization. The platform provides comprehensive
  cross-model benchmarking across XGBoost (standard and lightweight), tabular
  MLP, 1D-CNN, and Google Cloud AI TabNet architectures under real-world
  GPU-training and CPU-inference constraints.

